#!/usr/bin/python3
"""backup-vault (SFTP Backup Vault): SFTP accounts that can only add backups, and their rotation.

Backup accounts (the group sftp_backups) log in over SFTP, chrooted to /var/backups/sftp/<account>,
and can only add files under its upload/ folder: sshd refuses reading, deleting, links and copies
(/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/40-backup-vault.conf). Every minute `ingest` moves each finished upload out
of their reach into /var/backups/vault/<account> (root only, read-only and immutable) and records its
size and SHA-256. Every night `rotate` keeps a grandfather-father-son selection of each account's
backups and moves the rest to /var/backups/vault/.trash, which is emptied after some days.

Settings: /etc/backup-vault/backup-vault.conf. Guide: /etc/backup-vault/README.md and
https://github.com/MahdiGraph/SFTP-Backup-Vault (MIT licence).
"""

